course: dictionary
lesson: 14542
title: Pertinent details
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A pertinent detail is one that is closely connected to the subject and useful for it. Another word for pertinent is relevant. When you write an answer, choose the facts that really answer the question.
explain: «The report needs pertinent evidence, not every fact you can find.» Here pertinent means the evidence must link directly to the question. A fact about your favourite football team is interesting, but it is not pertinent to a report on rivers.
explain: To check if a detail is pertinent, ask: does this help answer the question? If yes, it is pertinent. If it only fills space, leave it out.
fact: Pertinent is an adjective. Its forms are pertinent, more pertinent and most pertinent.
fact: «Pertinent» means closely connected to the subject being talked about, and useful for it; relevant.
fact: «Pertinent to» shows what something is connected with: «The rain was pertinent to the flood.»
fact: «A pertinent question» goes straight to the point, so it helps everyone focus.
fact: The opposite of pertinent is irrelevant, which means not connected to the subject.
exercise: «Your answer must include pertinent evidence.» What does pertinent mean here? | *Closely linked to the question and useful for it | Very long and detailed | Funny and surprising | Written in pencil
exercise: «The judge asked a pertinent question.» What makes a question pertinent? | *It goes straight to the point | It is asked very quietly | It is about the weather
exercise: The essay asks why the river flooded. Which detail is pertinent? | My favourite colour is blue | I like eating toast for breakfast | *Heavy rain fell on the hills all night
test: «Only pertinent facts are needed in the report.» Which word means the same as pertinent? | *Relevant | Sleepy | Loud | Lovely
test: Which word is the opposite of pertinent? | Useful | *Irrelevant | Important | Clear
exam: Question: Why was the school closed on Monday? | My sister likes cats | *The school was closed because of the flood | The playground has new swings | Lunch was pasta
